Huh, you call it a reproducer but it is completely unrelated. It compiles fine if you put the make_tensor_descriptor call into the else branch of the constexpr if:
```python
    if isinstance(desc_or_ptr, tl.tensor_descriptor):
        return desc_or_ptr
    else:
        return tl.make_tensor_descriptor(desc_or_ptr, shape, strides, block_shape)
```

I don't see how this relates to getting NaNs though.

